{"name":"Windmill Wings","hex":"#f0f1ec","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"windmill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A machine which translates linear motion of wind to rotational motion by means of adjustable vanes called sails.","The building or structure containing such machinery."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rotate with a sweeping motion.","To (become disengaged and) rotate freely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windmill"},{"term":"wings","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wing"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of scuba harness with an attached buoyancy compensation device: see wikipedia:Backplate and wing","A flip (hairstyle)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wings"}],"entries":[{"title":"Windmill","blocks":[{"text":"A windmill is a machine operated by the force of wind acting on vanes or sails to mill grain (gristmills). Windmills were used throughout the high medieval and early modern periods; the horizontal or panemone windmill first appeared in Persia during the 9th century, and the vertical windmill first appeared in northwestern Europe in the 12th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/DK_Fanoe_Windmill01.JPG/330px-DK_Fanoe_Windmill01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windmill"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Heron%27s_Windwheel.png/500px-Heron%27s_Windwheel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Heron%27s_Windwheel.png/1280px-Heron%27s_Windwheel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Heron%27s_Windwheel.png/500px-Heron%27s_Windwheel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 19th-century reconstruction of Heron's wind-powered organ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeron's_Windwheel.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Margate_Hooper%27s_Mill.jpg/500px-Margate_Hooper%27s_Mill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Margate_Hooper%27s_Mill.jpg/1280px-Margate_Hooper%27s_Mill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Margate_Hooper%27s_Mill.jpg/500px-Margate_Hooper%27s_Mill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hooper's Mill, Margate, Kent, an eighteenth-century European horizontal windmill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMargate_Hooper's_Mill.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Windmill_in_Finland_in_1987_%281%29.jpg/500px-Windmill_in_Finland_in_1987_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Windmill_in_Finland_in_1987_%281%29.jpg/500px-Windmill_in_Finland_in_1987_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai